"A selectee is affixed by answering YES when asked to accept their duties as Avowed."
"Before affixation the interface calls the person a Pre-affixed Selectee."
"After accepting, the Avowed refines class options: foundation, skills, class info, privileges."
"Options not chosen when the grace period's hours run out are affixed at random."
"'Finalize affixation' completes it; some faint, rarely B-ranks, sometimes for many hours."
"Skill details stay hidden until chosen; the System can drop skills once quotas are met."
"A rare hard integration triggers special protocols to avoid creating an abomination."
"The System reports anomalies only past thresholds; violating spiritual privacy costs it debt."
"Authority by nature rejects limits on existence, and affixation is a profound limitation."
"One who can feel their authority never grows used to being affixed."
"A fresh affixation settles in for a while, vulnerable to damage; knights can feel this, Avowed not."
"Binding newly grown authority into skills costs the ability to cast spells for a time."
